-- the-guard-runs (2026-11-18, found while committing the chemistry construction): the pre-commit hook
-- (lib/guard.cub, run by the machine) is killed by the kernel before it finishes. Measured here: it
-- runs 2 minutes 32 seconds and dies of signal 9, its resident memory climbing to about 6.6 GB of the
-- machine's 8 GB — roughly 160 MB a second for the first 30 seconds, then slowly to the kill. The
-- machine was otherwise idle (716 MB used before the run), so this is the guard's own footprint and
-- not contention. It is reproducible: three runs, three kills.
-- What it costs: no agent can commit through the hook at the store's present size. The invariant the
-- guard exists to enforce — a commit holds nothing but the source (store/), CLAUDE.md, README.md and
-- the frozen files of its own g-frozen list — then has to be checked by hand (`git diff --cached
-- --name-only`) and the commit made with --no-verify, which is what was done for the chemistry
-- commits of 2026-11-18 and recorded in each of their messages. A guard that cannot run is a guard
-- that is not enforcing anything, so this is load-bearing and not housekeeping.
-- Where to look: the guard reads the whole source to check it, and the store has grown (16,769 objects
-- at this writing). Either the check is made streaming — each file's paths tested as it is read, with
-- nothing held — or the guard tests only the paths of the commit, which is all its rule needs: its
-- statement is about the names of the files a commit holds, not about their contents, except for the
-- byte-for-byte comparison of the frozen files, which can be done one file at a time.
-- 2026-11-18, later: it runs again (11 s), because its one-source check is out of its verdict (g-judge). That check
-- sorted every long prose line of the whole repository, so its cost was Θ(C log P) comparisons over the C
-- characters of P lines, all held at once: a global value materialized on one machine (memory-is-local). It
-- comes back as a lookup of the commit's new lines among the line hashes the store keeps, costing what the
-- commit holds and nothing of the rest.
the-guard-runs : Node
the-guard-runs = node "The pre-commit guard runs to completion within the machine's memory, so that a commit is checked rather than waved through: its rule is about the paths a commit holds and the bytes of the frozen files, and it is to be checked without holding the source." (cons the-product nil)
